n: 3.10.8.2
name: language-as-data-both-ways
kind: finding
is: A language enters as data over one engine in both directions: the rule that turns a node into text is data, as the grammar that parses text is. The old translator has the parsing half only; its decoders are code per language, so adding a language or a second construction is a programming task.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.10.1.1 3.10.1.8
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.10.8.3
